Linux-port HEVC speed (development record #379): drm/rockchip: lvds: keep the panel after bind.

Since 7.x rockchip_lvds_bind() drops its panel right after drm_panel_bridge_add_typed()
(drm_panel_put(), lvds->panel = NULL), yet it then replaces the new bridge's funcs with
rockchip_lvds_bridge_funcs, whose get_modes is drm_panel_get_modes(lvds->panel), and the
encoder's enable/disable prepare and enable lvds->panel. With the panel gone the bridge
connector has no modes, DRM falls back to 1024x768 (the board's panel showed the fbcon at
1024x768 on 7.3.1), and the panel is never prepared or enabled by DRM. Keep the panel and
its reference until unbind, as before the panel refcounting; the bind error path already
puts it.

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/rockchip/rockchip_lvds.c	2026-11-06 15:17:28.440993987 -0600
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/rockchip/rockchip_lvds.c	2026-11-06 15:17:28.450690495 -0600
@@ -727,8 +727,12 @@
 
 	if (lvds->panel) {
 		lvds->bridge = drm_panel_bridge_add_typed(lvds->panel, DRM_MODE_CONNECTOR_LVDS);
-		drm_panel_put(lvds->panel);
-		lvds->panel = NULL;
+		/*
+		 * Keep the panel (and its reference) until unbind: the bridge funcs below
+		 * replace the panel bridge's, so the connector's modes come from
+		 * rockchip_lvds_bridge_get_modes() and the panel is powered by the
+		 * encoder's enable/disable, all through lvds->panel.
+		 */
 		if (IS_ERR(lvds->bridge)) {
 			ret = PTR_ERR(lvds->bridge);
 			goto err_free_encoder;
@@ -783,6 +787,10 @@
 	encoder_funcs = lvds->soc_data->helper_funcs;
 	encoder_funcs->disable(&lvds->encoder.encoder);
 	pm_runtime_disable(dev);
+	if (lvds->panel) {
+		drm_panel_put(lvds->panel);
+		lvds->panel = NULL;
+	}
 }
 
 static const struct component_ops rockchip_lvds_component_ops = {
